  "why": "Ledger 3 holds the first transaction of the public network: the root account creates an account, pays it almost every lumen and sets its own master weight to 0, under a MEMO_TEXT \"hello world\" and in the pre-Protocol-13 ENVELOPE_TYPE_TX_V0 form whose source is a raw ed25519 key. The lake object is a recent stellar-core's re-emission, so this Protocol 1 ledger carries TransactionMeta v4 with backfilled transfer events whose to_muxed_id is the memo text. Readers that require V1 envelopes, that pick the meta layout from the protocol, or that turn the memo text into an address all fail on it.",
